+
+**Definition:** Signed distance to an equilateral triangle with inscribed radius $r$ [S2, unofficial].
+**Steps:**
+1.  Let $k = \sqrt{3.0}$ [S2, unofficial].
+2.  Transform $p_x = |p_x| - r$, $p_y = p_y + r/k$ [S2, unofficial].
+3.  If $p_x + k \cdot p_y > 0.0$, rotate: $p = ((p_x - k \cdot p_y)/2, (-k \cdot p_x - p_y)/2)$ [S2, unofficial].
+4.  Transform $p_x = p_x - \text{clamp}(p_x, -2r, 0)$ [S2, unofficial].
+5.  Return $-|p| \cdot \text{sign}(p_y)$ [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: $O(1)$. Constant number of arithmetic operations and comparisons.
-*   **Memory Complexity**: $O(1)$. No auxiliary data structures.
-*   **Strengths**: Extremely fast evaluation, suitable for real-time ray marching. Simple branching logic.
-*   **Limitations**: Only applies to regular octahedra. Not suitable for irregular polyhedra without modification.
-*   **Scaling**: Linear with respect to $s$.
